<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Albert Hahl</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1868–1945</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Albert Hahl was a German colonial administrator, governor of German <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-guinea">New Guinea</a> from 1902 to 1914. He extended administration through appointed village headmen, the luluai, and a head tax that pushed men into plantation labour, and he moved the capital to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rabaul">Rabaul</a> in 1910. He had earlier served as vice-governor in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caroline-islands">Caroline Islands</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/albert-hahl.jpg" alt="Albert Hahl" width="320" height="442" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Albert_Hahl_(cropped).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
